WEBVTT

00:00:00.103 --> 00:00:02.445
Not every concept needs its own table

00:00:04.187 --> 00:00:06.555
A concept often deserves a separate entity

00:00:06.581 --> 00:00:08.463
when it has its own identity several

00:00:08.489 --> 00:00:11.673
descriptive facts relationships to other concepts or

00:00:11.700 --> 00:00:15.857
is reused many times For example a

00:00:15.884 --> 00:00:17.779
service has a code a name a

00:00:17.805 --> 00:00:20.147
price and may appear in many appointments

00:00:21.071 --> 00:00:23.307
That makes service a strong candidate for

00:00:23.321 --> 00:00:27.554
its own table A simple attribute usually

00:00:27.580 --> 00:00:31.438
just describes another entity Birth date describes

00:00:31.465 --> 00:00:35.004
a patient Appointment start time describes an

00:00:35.030 --> 00:00:40.699
appointment Quantity describes one service line When

00:00:40.725 --> 00:00:43.133
deciding ask whether the concept needs to

00:00:43.159 --> 00:00:45.673
exist independently and be referenced by other

00:00:45.699 --> 00:00:48.662
records If not it may be better

00:00:48.675 --> 00:00:50.517
represented as a column rather than a

00:00:50.544 --> 00:00:51.438
separate table
